## Automation Policy

"Escalate P1s to L2 at 75%": when-clause + action + params, stored as data. THE HONEST LIMIT: the platform has no scheduler, so policies apply when a command runs, and every application is stamped (`lastAppliedAt`, `applyCount`) and attributed on the record's timeline as "by policy <name>" — automation never reads as a ghost.

```ts
import { AutomationPolicyField } from '@cardstack/catalog/fields/automation-policy/automation-policy-field';

@field policies = containsMany(AutomationPolicyField);
```

### Non-goals

No daemon, no cron, no notification on fire (the platform has no scheduler; the consumer's own board is the surface).
